[00:19.50]The greatest of men was our Lord Jesus Christ;
[00:26.10]By pride or ambition, he was not enticed.
[00:34.32]God’s purpose gave Jesus the prominent role;
[00:40.80]Yet, lowly in heart, he was always whole-souled.
[01:00.73]To all who are toiling with troublesome cares,
[01:07.59]He offers to carry the burdens they bear.
[01:15.22]Refreshment they find as the Kingdom they seek.
[01:22.36]With kindness and mildness, he favors the meek.
[01:39.36]‘We all are just brothers,’ our Lord Jesus said.
[01:45.90]In humble submission, we look to our Head.
[01:52.64]The mild and the meek ones to God have great worth;
[01:59.84]He promises they will inherit the earth.
